  "result": "Notes updated for season 6. Key findings this turn: confirmed FULL_DAY has never been scheduled in 5 seasons (permanently drop it), HD_AM/HD_PM stay dead across every ONI regime observed (0.06-0.08 yt/angler ceiling even in the best season), and strategy.py access is still absent. The big new insight: THREE_QUARTER's seasonal shape is regime-dependent, not calendar-fixed \u2014 deep La Ni\u00f1a seasons (S1/S2, which shaped my prior plan) cap out around 0.4-0.8 yt/angler with a narrow window, while warmer/rising-ONI seasons (S3-S5) produce broader, 3-8x larger peaks (1.5-3.5+/angler). Season 5 just ended with ONI still rising (+0.51), so S6 likely resembles the bigger warm-regime shape \u2014 I'll confirm once the first S6 ONI reading lands and recalibrate. I also flagged that the real S2 failure mode was PTO logistics (signals were live but unreachable because PTO wasn't pre-committed 14 days out), not signal detection \u2014 S6 plan now calls for a rolling 2-3-day PTO buffer through the active season instead of reactive commits.",
